                    text: "The national pipeline (114,000–144,000 rooms) turns into only about 15,000 net new rooms a year, so the risk is local. Horwath counts about 10,000 rooms planned in Bengaluru (+53%), 6,000 under way in east Mumbai and Navi Mumbai (+34%), new supply at Delhi's Aerocity and Yashobhoomi, and an analyst on Brigade's call cited about 5,000 premium rooms planned in Hyderabad by 2032. That touches **Chalet** (Mumbai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad), **Juniper** (Aerocity, Bengaluru), **Brigade** (Bengaluru, Hyderabad) and **Viceroy** (Hyderabad). It has already happened twice: **Lemon Tree**'s Aurika Mumbai had flat RevPAR after about 2,000 rooms opened near the airport, and **Royal Orchid**'s Iconiqa opened alongside about 1,000 new rooms. South Mumbai, central Delhi, Chennai and Pune luxury, where **EIH**, **Leela** and **Ventive** are strongest, stay tight.",
